Rogues can get Skilled in both of those weapon categories. And you will
very quickly become Basic, which is the precondition that you don't get
the to-hit penalty.

> Is stormbringer really that good?

As I said, it's one of the best. In addition to the normal damage it
drains life (if monsters are not from the Undead monster classes) and
thus reduces additional HPs. According to the analysis in the spoilers
(http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/art2-343.txt) it is one of the
three best weapons for Rogues in the early game (and certainly also
good enough in the late game).

> [...] I've heard that armor can only be enchanted
> up to +4 before additional enchantments may desintegrate it,

Armor can be enchanted safely once(!) when at +3; so with a blessed
scroll it can get either +4 or +5 that way.

> but I've
> also heard that some armor is excepted from this rule and can go up to
> +6 (and thus up to +7 if you're lucky enough with a blessed scroll).

Elven armor (and a cornuthaum, AFAIR) can be enchanted even when at +5.

> Dragon scale mail is one of the ones that can go up to +7 safely,
> right?

No. Dragon scales can be enchanted once more if at +3, thus possibly
getting either +4 or +5 with a blessed scroll.

> I forgot to mention that I was also lucky enough to get intrinsic
> speed from my god after doing a holy water prayer... does that stack
> with the boots?

Boots will make you always "very fast", whether you have intrinsic speed
(i.e. being "fast") or not. It does not accumulate.

