>>> 13,059 zorkmids
>>
>> Buy as much protection as possible as long as you are low level; you
>> can get 9 points of intrinsic protection easily. The rest of the gold
>> is just useless weight after you've visited all shops. In the late game
>> you need just a few bucks to bribe some demons.
> 
> I heard something about bribing the demons; how much do they ask for,
> exactly?

That's really silly; they only ask for a part of what you carry in open
inventory. So if you carry 10 Zorkmids thay ask not more than that. But
you should *have* the money, otherwise they get angry. OTOH, you have a
turn free to take the money from your bag when they appear. Only two of
the guaranteed demons seem to accept money, Asmodeus and Baalzebub. And
alignment also matters, I think; as a chaotic Rogue you may not get the
chance to bribe them. And also if you carry Excalibur in your inventory
they get mad at you.

>>> So here are my questions: First of all, do I have a descent chance of
>>> ascending?
>>
>> Yes, but having MR is crucial! You have practically no chance without.
> 
> Looking for GDSM, can't find any other source at the moment.

That's fine. In case you don't get scales just wish for that armor. And
beware the major spell-casters until you've got MR.

>>> Second, should I raid Fort Ludios before I do my quest or after?
>>
>> For Ludios you should have reflection; don't do it without. (An option
>> could be wielding a cockatrice.) I'd do Ludios only in case I'd need
>> gold, which you don't seem to need, or dragon armor, but there I'd
>> prefer to first seek in the Castle.
> 
> Wielding a cockatrice gives you reflection?

No. But when you place yourself on a good spot and are fast enough you
can stone the whole area with a fresh corpse; just stand close behind
the door to the inner area, a knights-move away and wait for the soldiers
to show up. But mind that it is very risky without both, reflection and
MR, because they frequently happen offensive wands, and a wand of death
may be amongst those. OTOH, with MR or reflection you'll get all their
wands (quite) fully charged if you use a cockatrice corpse.

